                <pb facs="0386" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/826c.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson informs Mr. Reid that in view of favorable reception by French
                    Government and group of the proposal contained in the department’s telegram of
                    February 8, he will present the substance of that instruction formally to the
                    British Government and urge an early settlement of this question on the basis of
                    the American proposal, which now appears to be acceptable to all the other
                    interests concerned. Mr. Reid is directed to repeat this telegram to the
                    American Embassies at Berlin and Paris for their information.</p>
            </div>
